# /etc/menu -- entries for usr.bin/menu, the full-screen menu launcher.
#
# One entry per line: "label: command". A blank line or a line starting
# with '#' is skipped. The command runs through /bin/sh -c, so pipes and
# redirection work. usr.bin/menu already offers three built-in actions
# (run a program, show a file with the pager, list a directory) ahead of
# this file's entries; add a line here for anything else worth one
# keypress from the console.
Show disk usage: df
Show processes: ps
Show the date: date
Show system name: uname -a
